# SceneManager

Namespace Axiom.Gameplay.SceneManagement. Scenes are physical project JSON files ending .scene.json with {"format":"axiom-scene","version":1,"entities":[...]}. Their authored local hierarchy is converted to world transforms and imported with remapped identities. Scene resources share already prepared project assets and compiled scripts; they do not open a different editor project. Name-only paths must be unambiguous. At most 16 runtime scenes, 64 runtime creations per Play generation, 65536 entities and 32 live scripts; repeated loads consume the creation budget. No disk authoring changes occur during Play.

LoadScene Single destroys nonpersistent root objects and descendants; Additive preserves existing objects. DontDestroyOnLoad marks a root subtree. CreateScene, GetActiveScene, SetActiveScene, MoveGameObjectToScene, unload and root queries track ownership. An existing scene cannot be loaded twice additively. LoadSceneAsync returns a completed operation because resource data is already resident; rendering applies the validated packet at the next host boundary. Streaming, background I/O, scene lighting settings, asset bundles and Addressables are pending. Persistent roots retain their old owner; this version does not display a dedicated DontDestroyOnLoad scene group.

```csharp
using Axiom.Gameplay.SceneManagement;
SceneManager.LoadScene("Arena", LoadSceneMode.Additive);
var arena = SceneManager.GetSceneByName("Arena");
Debug.Log(arena.rootCount);
SceneManager.UnloadSceneAsync("Arena");
```

Use Scenes & Resources API Lab. Scene source scripts must belong to the current compiled project bundle.

SDK 8: ordinary Play starts the active authored scene plus explicitly Always active scenes. `SetSceneAlwaysActive(Scene,bool)` and `IsSceneAlwaysActive(Scene)` are **Axiom extensions**, not Unity members. A flagged scene survives LoadScene(Single); UnloadSceneAsync rejects it until its flag is cleared. Objects from these scenes share the runtime and may reference one another. Editor scene order and pinning are saved and undoable. A scene header remains separate in runtime Hierarchy.

